{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview","id":1539594,"title":"W5 Shattered Nation - Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-31T10:15:56-07:00","id":1539594,"title":"W5 Shattered Nation - Preview","content":"Renegade released a preview of the upcoming W5 supplement &quot;Shattered Nation&quot; that has a section from the Introduction. The text presents the pitch of the book and what it is about<b></b>:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"2048\" height=\"1310\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/DZcUfVw.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/DZcUfVw.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/DZcUfVw.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> The text just reminds me why I have never been a fan of &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen&quot; and especially not in the wishy-washy way it was presented in the W5 corebook. This description is just such a mess in terms of worldbuilding.<ul><li>The idea of something entering the realm of myth within one generation is so strange - especially while living people are around who still remember it.</li> <li>It says &quot;Older Garou have proven that they don't have what it takes...&quot;, okay... but they're still around. They can still take action. If we're going with the idea that the Fall happened in living memory, then things certainly can still be turned around by these people. I get the idea of condemning the failings of distant previous generations but old people who are still alive and able to take action...? They will still play a role in the local setting. And it's not like they're frail old humans in a retirement-home. We're talking about Garou here.</li> <li>The Garou used to be able to work together - but also in the age of modern communication, the Garou found out (and why modern communication... no Garou ever talked to another Garou beyond the local level before then...?!) that everybody's doing things differently locally...? Then why did they all call themselves Garou, for example? This feels like the worst way to explain what the challenge of reforming/rebuilding the Garou Nation is. Also, this implies the pitch of a rebuilt Garou Nation should be to bulldoze local traditions...? Because why else would this be described as a challenge? Just such a bizarre paragraph...</li> <li>If everything's local and nothing's universal... then wouldn't it make more sense in that framework for Tribes to be tied to specific people and/or regions...? Using this framework wouldn't you just recreate the old Tribes again, Egyptian Silent Striders, Russian Silver Fangs, Greek Black Furies etc.</li> <li>Hopefully this book has more of a global perspective and gives examples of Garou-traditions from all around the world. Because it's hard to take this local focus seriously when all the adventures that have been released thus far were located in North America.</li> </ul><br /> This certainly has lowered my expectations for the supplement. It's like somebody just thoughtlessly threw all the typical WOD5E and W5 tropes together: street-level-only, lore is bad (nobody knows anything for some reason), old Garou are bad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27535,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","user":"Knightingale","date":". 07-31-2024, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T22:30:31-07:00","id":1539620,"title":"","content":"Okay but there is a question you are not asking, Knight; If the Nation isn't moots, if it isn't septs and packs guarding them... then what WAS it?<br /> <br /> Because the scenario presented in the text does not differ from how things were done during the Nation days. Moots alone imply that there is communication between the garou of the area, enough to gather every full moon to tell tales.<br /> <br /> I think the question of the book shouldn't be how the Nation fell, but what it actually was in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T23:40:31-07:00","id":1539624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539620#post1539620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but there is a question you are not asking, Knight; If the Nation isn't moots, if it isn't septs and packs guarding them... then what WAS it?<br /> <br /> Because the scenario presented in the text does not differ from how things were done during the Nation days. Moots alone imply that there is communication between the garou of the area, enough to gather every full moon to tell tales.<br /> <br /> I think the question of the book shouldn't be how the Nation fell, but what it actually was in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta know where you're coming from in order to inform where you're going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T01:29:25-07:00","id":1539625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539620#post1539620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but there is a question you are not asking, Knight; If the Nation isn't moots, if it isn't septs and packs guarding them... then what WAS it?<br /> <br /> Because the scenario presented in the text does not differ from how things were done during the Nation days. Moots alone imply that there is communication between the garou of the area, enough to gather every full moon to tell tales.<br /> <br /> I think the question of the book shouldn't be how the Nation fell, but what it actually was in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three things this book hopefully addresses:<ul><li>What was the Garou-Nation like before it fell?</li> <li>Make a convincing case for how the Garou-Nation fell (How did it happen? What events led up to it? What was the breaking point?)</li> <li>What is Garou-life like now after the Fall? What makes it different from how things were before?</li> </ul>From the way it's described, I assume the &quot;breaking point&quot;-event will be that &quot;last disastrous concolation&quot; headed by King Albrecht and it's probably the same one where the Cult of Fenris guys come to blows with the rest of the Nation. I guess we'll see how convincing it is as a breaking point.<br /> <br /> But rereading the text, I've been thinking... One wild swing and huge change you could make in the way it's phrased is to say that all the Tribes only came into existence <i>after </i>the Fall. So, a hundred years ago there hadn't even been anything like a Tribe in the Garou Nation. And the Tribes in this version of the W5 setting are just divergent ideas of how to tackle the problems of the world without any bigger history. Is that consistent with how Tribes have even been described in other W5 material? Not really but I've been getting the sense with what has been released thus far, this isn't a priority for W5 anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T03:28:13-07:00","id":1539630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539625#post1539625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But rereading the text, I've been thinking... One wild swing and huge change you could make in the way it's phrased is to say that all the Tribes only came into existence <i>after </i>the Fall. So, a hundred years ago there hadn't even been anything like a Tribe in the Garou Nation. And the Tribes in this version of the W5 setting are just divergent ideas of how to tackle the problems of the world without any bigger history..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That pretty similar premises to <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ec258PrLWeU0F-Yy6tUy6lmkTVtX7Rud/view\" target=\"_blank\">werewolf punk remix</a> that's posted a few months back.<br /> <br /> Like in this game the version of the garou nation has fallen a long time ago and only recently did new wolves come into existence (the text out right says the oldest known instance of the first change is a decade ago).and the tribes are presented as more informal groups bounded tougher by a strong belief a phosphines that backed by a patron sprit (called Tutelary.in the book). Than a proper cultures..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T03:31:34-07:00","id":1539686,"title":"","content":"Tribes are definitely one of those things in the W5 corebook that could've needed an extra-dose of &quot;re-imagining&quot;. And the idea of Tribes only coming into existence after the Fall because they're essentially divergent ideas of what to do makes more sense than what you get from the corebook. It also fits into the goal of making the Tribes more universal. So it's strange that the text also emphasizes the differences between local settings. On pg 232 of the W5 corebook in the Spirit Veracity sidebar, it says: &quot;So, for example, a Ghost Council Garou with a Native American background may well perceive Horned Serpent in a different way than fellow Ghost Council Garou living amid Scandinavian, Iranian, or North African human cultures. Through the Garou lens, all of them are true, all of them are \u201cthe\u201d Horned Serpent, even if all of them are different.&quot; That's why it's strange that this text is presenting it as a challenge. Because if you follow the logic of the W5 corebook, two Garou from two different locales should realize that they may have different names for these things but deep down they're both doing the same thing and have the same traditions. But what this text from Shattered Nation suggests is that you wouldn't have two Garou who while having different names for things belong to the Ghost Council Tribe and have the Horned Serpent as their Tribe-Patron-Spirit. What this proposes instead is that the two Garou talk to each other and they don't just have different names for stuff, they are of two different Tribes with different beliefs and practices and they have two different Tribe-Patron-Spirits.<br /> <br /> Then again, tying things to the specifics of a locale is certainly one way you can enforce the street-level-only design-goal of WOD5E... It just would have been nice if they could've fulfilled their design-goals without contradicting themselves like this.<br /> <br /> The same goes for the question of why the Garou-Nation is considered fallen... I'm sure one of the central ideas of this book is to play out a campaign that is attached to the &quot;Your PC is King Albrecht's newest BFF&quot;-Loresheet. But if King Albrecht is still around, if the old Garou who were at that disastrous gathering are also still around, if there are still a bunch of Garou all over the world living in Septs and having Moots... then in what way has the Garou Nation fallen apart? All the ingredients that used to make it tick are still around. It's not like King Albrecht died over a hundred years ago and nobody knows where the Silver Crown is.<br /> <br /> Also, this could be another scenario where the Fenrir are just coming off as more sensible. If this is the gathering where the Fenrir had their hissy-fit, complained about the other Garou, got really angry and then left... Wouldn't the Fenrir be proven correct, if after all of that King Albrecht just gave up and and all the other Garou just went back to their caerns to mope till the world's end...? King Albrecht and the other supposedly &quot;good Garou&quot; would really come off like a bunch of losers if confronted by the angry Fenrir urging them to action, they just react with a shrug saying &quot;Shit happens. I guess we've failed.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T23:20:19-07:00","id":1539737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539686#post1539686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, this could be another scenario where the Fenrir are just coming off as more sensible. If this is the gathering where the Fenrir had their hissy-fit, complained about the other Garou, got really angry and then left... Wouldn't the Fenrir be proven correct, if after all of that King Albrecht just gave up and and all the other Garou just went back to their caerns to mope till the world's end...? King Albrecht and the other supposedly &quot;good Garou&quot; would really come off like a bunch of losers if confronted by the angry Fenrir urging them to action, they just react with a shrug saying &quot;Shit happens. I guess we've failed.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well compare that to what WtE's version of Albrecht did during the apocalypse:<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/79jLPWY.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/79jLPWY.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/79jLPWY.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/AGECO8l.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/AGECO8l.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/AGECO8l.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> He and his pack is able to seal Storm Eater deep in the umbra at the cost of trapping them selves in with it. Aborting (or at least heavily delaying) the Apocalypse and he even relay the last words of gaia herself to the rest of the garou nation. Inspiring some hope for the new generation.<br /> <br /> <br /> One wonders if W5 is actually a wyrm made illusion that's collectively experienced by Albrecht and his pack while trapped in the deep umbra showing the garous at they worst. In a effort to break them and make them turn to the wyrm. And of course it's up to a new generation of new garou heroes to break into said illusion and free the garou king from the false world that imprisons him in an adventure that really lean into gnostic themes of WtA (I mean one of the stats is Gnosis... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T10:36:10-07:00","id":1539863,"title":"","content":"Matt Stormcrow (he's a WOD-fan-content-creator primarily on TikTok, it seems... don't know his work) talked to Kevin Schluter (he's from Renegade and a Producer for their RPG-books) about Shattered Nation. The video can be found <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mattstormcrow/video/7398876095883316522\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. While they're talking, they're flipping through the book. I didn't take the time to pause the video and look too closely at the pages. I will read the whole thing anyway in a couple of weeks whenever the preview-pdf comes out.<br /> <br /> But some takeaways from what I glimpsed:<ul><li>Pack-Types are done in the way that I hoped! They're an analogue to Coterie-Types.</li> <li>Sept-positions are back. It looked like it's pretty much everything from the previous editions plus some new additions like &quot;Sheepwolf&quot; (the Garou in charge of interacting with humans).</li> <li>There's a whole chapter dedicated to explaining the relationship between Garou and humans in a world without Kinfolk.</li> <li>Septs vary in how they relate to other Septs. I guess, that's part of that whole local focus that was already part of the excerpt I posted above. Hmm, that's the part that doesn't quite sit right with me. Because if the setting really leans into Garou being super-factionalized (where the divisions run so deep that they express themselves on a Sept-level) then there's no reason for the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers to stand out/be unplayable and for the Cult in particular to be this demonized extraordinary antagonist.</li> <li>There were quite a few pages with just fluff in-character texts. If the writing's good, this could be good. W5 could use more flavor.</li> <li>There's a section about age-groups in Garou-society... Hmm... Hopefully it doesn't just end up being a &quot;Old Garou are bad. Period.&quot;-explainer.</li> <li>Just as an aside, I wonder if this book will be more about the new lead-developer and the Renegade-team announcing that this is what <i>they </i>want W5 to be like in contrast to what is presented in the W5 corebook.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T15:25:58-07:00","id":1539891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539863#post1539863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt Stormcrow (he's a WOD-fan-content-creator primarily on TikTok, it seems... don't know his work) talked to Kevin Schluter (he's from Renegade and a Producer for their RPG-books) about Shattered Nation. The video can be found <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@mattstormcrow/video/7398876095883316522\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. While they're talking, they're flipping through the book. I didn't take the time to pause the video and look too closely at the pages. I will read the whole thing anyway in a couple of weeks whenever the preview-pdf comes out.<br /> <br /> But some takeaways from what I glimpsed:<br /> <br /> Pack-Types are done in the way that I hoped! They're an analogue to Coterie-Types.<br /> Sept-positions are back. It looked like it's pretty much everything from the previous editions plus some new additions like &quot;Sheepwolf&quot; (the Garou in charge of interacting with humans).</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Sheepwolf&quot; strikes me as a blatant copy of a post typically given to various vampire societies, and seems counter to the lore - if the Garou had a dedicated version of that, they probably wouldn't have fallen so far behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a whole chapter dedicated to explaining the relationship between Garou and humans in a world without Kinfolk. </div> </div> </div>I suspect the ability to soft-quit being a Garou by losing the wolf and not howling again plays into this (speaking of inconsistent lore not supporting the setting...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Septs vary in how they relate to other Septs. I guess, that's part of that whole local focus that was already part of the excerpt I posted above. Hmm, that's the part that doesn't quite sit right with me. Because if the setting really leans into Garou being super-factionalized (where the divisions run so deep that they express themselves on a Sept-level) then there's no reason for the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers to stand out/be unplayable and for the Cult in particular to be this demonized extraordinary antagonist. </div> </div> </div>A byproduct of wanting to be street-level only but having to try and incorporate non-street material because otherwise there isn't much left flavor-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There were quite a few pages with just fluff in-character texts. If the writing's good, this could be good. W5 could use more flavor.<br /> There's a section about age-groups in Garou-society... Hmm... Hopefully it doesn't just end up being a &quot;Old Garou are bad. Period.&quot;-explainer.<br /> Just as an aside, I wonder if this book will be more about the new lead-developer and the Renegade-team announcing that this is what <i>they </i>want W5 to be like in contrast to what is presented in the W5 corebook. </div> </div> </div>I'm not expecting the impressive cleanup that SR6 managed, mostly because W5 was way deeper in the hole from the start. Digging your way out of that mess is going to take more than a revised core and a neat companion book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T19:54:00-07:00","id":1539911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1539863#post1539863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Septs vary in how they relate to other Septs. I guess, that's part of that whole local focus that was already part of the excerpt I posted above. Hmm, that's the part that doesn't quite sit right with me. Because if the setting really leans into Garou being super-factionalized (where the divisions run so deep that they express themselves on a Sept-level) then there's no reason for the Cult of Fenris and the Stargazers to stand out/be unplayable and for the Cult in particular to be this demonized extraordinary antagonist.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that's somewhat close to how lodges work in Forsaken. At least in the sense that there's really divergent culturally even if they belong to the same tribe. Though I don't know if they actually infight that much compared to the garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T22:57:15-07:00","id":1539916,"title":"","content":"The Generations things with garou only garouing for 10 years after change is... weird. Yes, the turnover has always been brutal, but you'd think with there no longer being any pressure to dedicate your life to the sept, the age range would broaden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T15:45:53-07:00","id":1539954,"title":"","content":"Some of these concepts are interesting in that I could see cribbing then over to earlier editions. For example, I don\u2019t play V5, but I do crib some things from like Coterie Types, Feeding Types, Lore Sheets, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T12:45:15-07:00","id":1540004,"title":"","content":"And here's another preview that makes me feel less hopeful again... The first two pages of the &quot;Among Wolves&quot;-chapter: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1246\" height=\"795\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/UpUA2zN.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/UpUA2zN.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/UpUA2zN.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><ul><li>The first couple of paragraphs in Layers just feel like a waste of space. The hierarchy of &quot;Pack - Sept - Tribe - (in the past) Garou-Nation&quot; had already been covered by the corebook. And as it points out, you'd think the smallest social unit would be the individual if you were to go by present-day modern viewpoints - so why isn't that the case in Garou-society? And what does that mean exactly? That's what needs to be covered. You don't need yet another superficial look at Garou society like the one mentioned here. And sure maybe the book will go into more detail on this later on. But you're still looking at a couple dozen words on this page here that were absolutely unnecessary and didn't add anything of worth.</li> <li>The Garou-Nation-skepticism still irks me. It always reads like somebody's ill-informed opinion that history before 1800 is just a bunch of hearsay and fairytales. Along with weird statements like &quot;at a time when humans had barely managed to get from one continent to another&quot;. Okay, that was a long, LONG time ago and humans had been getting better at it ever since and for continents that were better positioned (like Europe, Africa and Asia) there have been strong connections for thousands of years.</li> <li>Also, who cares when &quot;humans&quot; were barely able to do this or that... We're not talking about humans here, we're talking about Garou/werewolves. This is a setting with supernatural elements! This is a setting where Spirits are real! Good fantastical settings work best when supernatural elements are employed in imaginative and creative ways. &quot;How could there have been a global Garou-Nation when humans were barely able to travel between continents?&quot; feels like the opposite of that. It feels more like somebody's argument for why they reject the setting/premise of this game. I don't think you win any points by allowing arguments like this and then just cover it up by saying &quot;Who even knows what's true...&quot;. This just undermines the premise of the game.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T13:25:25-07:00","id":1540006,"title":"","content":"In the vein of Knightingale\u2019s skepticism above, if the concept of the Garou Nation is suspect because of the limitations of human communication, then how are the tribes still accepted as the larger social grouping above the Sept level? What is the tribe then? How is tribal identity organized or defined?<br /> <br /> That aside, I do think there\u2019s good room to be delved into the social relations of Garou and what it would mean for Garou society to posit groups as the basic unit of society rather then the individual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T13:53:30-07:00","id":1540009,"title":"","content":"Many of W5s aspects feel like rejecting a premise and then trying to find reasons after the fact.....which is why none of the reasons given are actually good or compelling ones.....I had hoped this trend would be over by now but it seems to be continuing despite the partial change in Developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T14:16:43-07:00","id":1540012,"title":"","content":"Okay but once more, they are presenting the basic Legacy situation and then treating the Nation as somehow different from that. Are we talking about this huge mono-tribe that spanned continents?<br /> <br /> Also, yet again oral and pre-industrial history are ignored. We know of Ea-Nasir the copper seller from ancient Babylon, but garou can't remember stuff a couple of generations ago?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T14:20:47-07:00","id":1540013,"title":"","content":"I don't get the point of Garou-Nation-skepticism. I had hoped we had left this nonsense behind with the corebook. Especially at this point. The supplement is called &quot;Shattered Nation&quot;. It's supposed to be about what the fallen Garou-Nation is like. Why waste any wordcount on how the existence of the Garou Nation is disputed...? You can't do &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen.&quot; and &quot;Some believe the Garou Nation never existed to begin with.&quot; at the same time.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, I'm wrong but I'm dreading what this could mean for how they approach the worldbuilding... Like every fifth paragraph the writers feel the need to remind the reader that &quot;Hey, some say... maybe none of what was said in the last couple paragraphs is true.&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T14:51:08-07:00","id":1540015,"title":"","content":"Some say that Vampire mains are the worst choice to write Werewolf books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T17:38:07-07:00","id":1540021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540013#post1540013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully, I'm wrong but I'm dreading what this could mean for how they approach the worldbuilding... Like every fifth paragraph the writers feel the need to remind the reader that &quot;Hey, some say... maybe none of what was said in the last couple paragraphs is true.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well by contrast here's how WtE presents the fall of the garou nation:<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Like in less than two pages it establishes the foundation of the Eastern Concordat, how the apocalypse went down and how the garou nation actually split.(in short it's a lack of strong leader ship in a time of crises and existing tenstions between the tribes boiling over).<br /> <br /> Again all of this is said in two pages without the narrative doubling back and saying &quot;it might not be real&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude18","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T15:20:23-07:00","id":1540066,"title":"","content":"I could easily make 'The Garou Nation has fallen and modern Garou know barely anything about it's work in the classic lore. Sure it involves killing off the vast majority of Garou and forcing the next generation to learn from kinfolk, whatever written records do exist, and the few Garou not important enough to be at the opening of the Apocalypse, but I could do it.<br /> <br /> W5 Lore just seems confused and overly critical of anything that Western culture in the last few hundred years didn't do. It insists that oral history can't record events that happened a decade ago when my family has longer oral records than that and some cultures have passed down lore via the spoken word for millennia. The idea that the Romans might have traded with China? Ridiculous!<br /> <br /> Which isn't even my biggest problem with it (bring back Kinfolk and Chinos,-born, they had a role in the commentary). But W5 feels like it's shouting 'the game is global now' while quietly making everything European/American.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T17:32:56-07:00","id":1540069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540066#post1540066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily make 'The Garou Nation has fallen and modern Garou know barely anything about it's work in the classic lore. Sure it involves killing off the vast majority of Garou and forcing the next generation to learn from kinfolk, whatever written records do exist, and the few Garou not important enough to be at the opening of the Apocalypse, but I could do it.<br /> <br /> W5 Lore just seems confused and overly critical of anything that Western culture in the last few hundred years didn't do. It insists that oral history can't record events that happened a decade ago when my family has longer oral records than that and some cultures have passed down lore via the spoken word for millennia. The idea that the Romans might have traded with China? Ridiculous!<br /> <br /> Which isn't even my biggest problem with it (bring back Kinfolk and Chinos,-born, they had a role in the commentary). But W5 feels like it's shouting 'the game is global now' while quietly making everything European/American.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sitting in a country with 60K+ years worth of oral history looking at W5s attitude with utter derision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T22:23:02-07:00","id":1540074,"title":"","content":"So on a related note the preview for WtE's final lay out is out and I've put up a thread covering it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\"> WtE Final layout Preview - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540073-wte-final-layout-preview </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Well as it says on the tin this is the Preview for the final layout of Book 1 of the (Hopefully) five book run of Werewolf the Essentials. Source: https://www.tumblr.com/werewolfessentials/758186097516871680/for-todays-werewolf-wednesday-rather-than?source=share There's not much else to say that I haven't said before </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So if anyone want pop by and contrast and compare then be my guest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T02:49:42-07:00","id":1540076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540069#post1540069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sitting in a country with 60K+ years worth of oral history looking at W5s attitude with utter derision.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5 is utterly laughable, and not in a good way.<br /> <br /> The sad thing is there's many ways they could salvage it, including the possibility that the lore is there but young Garou just don't care.<br /> <br /> Honestly I also find it hard to believe that no Tribes would have written records. Going beyond the efforts of individual Garou at minimum the Glasswalkers almost certainly have been writing things down for hundreds of years, albeit likely encoded, and they'll have thousands of hard drives and servers packed with information.<br /> <br /> Basically the premise of W5 only works if the Garou Nation fell at minimum centuries ago, the Garou were incompetents who didn't bother to pass their knowledge along, or the PCs are unlikely to meet any Garou who remember the Nation.<br /> <br /> Hell the implied idea behind the Garou Nation falling and needing a replacement is solid, it's the conflict between the action required on a local scale versus what's actually needed to fix the global problem*. But it feels like the original developers didn't want to put in the legwork of explaining why the Nation was bad. Which leads to this bizarre situation where the local Elders are seemingly sitting around moping and refusing to actually speak to younger Garou.<br /> <br /> Except for the Cult of Fenris who'd make a good set of extremist antagonists if the other Garou were actually gluing themselves to the road or whatever. As it is they're leaning on alt-right imagery that's mostly tangential to the environmental themes.<br /> <br /> * My favourite bit of Book of Hungry Names is where it turns out that the pipeline your old pack fought against merely got rerouted out of their territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T04:23:11-07:00","id":1540078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540076#post1540076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Basically the premise of W5 only works if the Garou Nation fell at minimum centuries ago, the Garou were incompetents who didn't bother to pass their knowledge along, or the PCs are unlikely to meet any Garou who remember the Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly what Werewolf Punk remix does <br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/IzCBDdu.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/IzCBDdu.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/IzCBDdu.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/> <br /> Like the above post out right says the current generation of werewolf would at most have 10 years of experience of being a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell the implied idea behind the Garou Nation falling and needing a replacement is solid, it's the conflict between the action required on a local scale versus what's actually needed to fix the global problem*. </div> </div> </div>Well in WtE that's basically a reason for the Eastern Concordat to from and later split from the nation. Of course even then It's implied that the Western slowly came to the same conclusion and are slowly starting to make changes to they methods. <br /> <br /> And I should note that the split was purely political and is brought on by the fact that garou nation lack a leader in a time of great political turmoil because Albrecht was busy being trapped in the deep Umbra. Like there is a chance that the split didn't happen or at least delayed if things went differently but at the time that it's happening it's uncertain. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T07:40:35-07:00","id":1540083,"title":"","content":"W5's priorities are just not that well-aligned with what WtA is. They have this focus on humanity, for example. So you have your warehouse with abusive working-conditions or a hunting company or some other industry-site like an oil refinery or pipeline. Then you reveal to the players that a ), it's a bad thing and b ), the leadership and security personnel are all Fomori. Then the PCs do their thing, go in, destroy the thing, kill the Fomori, earn Renown... It's the &quot;radical goth-punk game of environmental horror where you can finally do something&quot; (that's the way it's presented occasionally). But then W5 is just so proud of itself, it thinks it's just so profound to then point out how this one action hasn't solved climate-change, hasn't truly fixed the underlying issue and doesn't it say SO MUCH about the flawed nature of Garou that their Rage hasn't solved everything magically? Except the W5-setup is rather than profound quite banal. You put a bad thing in the setting, the proverbial nail that sticks out and needs to be dealt with, you put a hammer in the form of Garou-warriors into the hands of the players, they use the hammer on the nail and then W5 thinks it's interesting to point out that not everything in the world can be solved with a hammer - except the solution is always the hammer because that's what W5 gives to the players. There hasn't been a single W5 adventure that hasn't culminated in &quot;And now the PCs have to kick this big bad guy's ass.&quot;. Therefore, what W5 perceives as profound only even exists on the level of when you talk <i>about </i>the game not in the way that it plays and what happens during the game.<br /> <br /> But you could reframe it as &quot;The world has been getting worse, the Wyrm has been getting stronger and if it's a contest between Bane-Spirits/Fomori/Pentex/BSD and humanity then humanity is gonna lose. That's why you need Garou.&quot;. You can't do that, though, because that would put the focus more on the Wyrm than bad humans which in turn would make things more spiritual again, give the Umbra a bigger focus. And Paradox doesn't want that.<br /> <br /> Also, my suspicion is that lore-wise this supplement will be a let-down overall. Because ultimately W5 doesn't like WtA-lore. &quot;Re-imagination, not continuation&quot; and all that... If any writer were to go too far in re-introducing old bits of lore, that's where then these paragraphs appear that argue stuff like &quot;Maybe the Garou Nation never existed, ever considered that?&quot; to counter-balance things. It will just be this tug-of-war between writers trying to add anything of substance to the setting but then having to adhere to the idea that WtA-lore is bad and needs to be avoided. And yet, since W5 also isn't a huge departure a la WtF, the old lore is the most obvious thing to add to the game. Like, trying to explain Septs... easiest way to do that is to just pick up the WtA 20th Anniversary and do a copy-paste. Similarly, in online-conversations when new players asked about clarifications and more lore... the easiest way to deal with that has been to just refer them back to the previous editions. But my suspicion/fear is that there's just this editorial stance coming from Paradox that looks at a supplement like this one and would have insisted on making sure WtA-lore is avoided/undermined as much as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-09T07:59:15-07:00","id":1540084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540083#post1540083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5's priorities are just not that well-aligned with what WtA is. They have this focus on humanity, for example. So you have your warehouse with abusive working-conditions or a hunting company or some other industry-site like an oil refinery or pipeline. Then you reveal to the players that a ), it's a bad thing and b ), the leadership and security personnel are all Fomori. Then the PCs do their thing, go in, destroy the thing, kill the Fomori, earn Renown... It's the &quot;radical goth-punk game of environmental horror where you can finally do something&quot; (that's the way it's presented occasionally). But then W5 is just so proud of itself, it thinks it's just so profound to then point out how this one action hasn't solved climate-change, hasn't truly fixed the underlying issue and doesn't it say SO MUCH about the flawed nature of Garou that their Rage hasn't solved everything magically? Except the W5-setup is rather than profound quite banal. You put a bad thing in the setting, the proverbial nail that sticks out and needs to be dealt with, you put a hammer in the form of Garou-warriors into the hands of the players, they use the hammer on the nail and then W5 thinks it's interesting to point out that not everything in the world can be solved with a hammer - except the solution is always the hammer because that's what W5 gives to the players. There hasn't been a single W5 adventure that hasn't culminated in &quot;And now the PCs have to kick this big bad guy's ass.&quot;. Therefore, what W5 perceives as profound only even exists on the level of when you talk <i>about </i>the game not in the way that it plays and what happens during the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition, W5 isn't even willing to move from the WtA structure to one where its more 'nuanced' conflicts would shine. It STILL expects combat and still expects killing. As you said, it sets up a nail and offers a hammer and then insults the players for using the hammer.<br /> <br /> But I think more than all of that, your point about W5 working as intended in the abstract is telling. When you look at the mechanics and the actual gameplay, it only offers a worse version of the W20 experience. There is no adventure that offers any other choice but killing, there is no peaceful solution available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T09:36:22-07:00","id":1540365,"title":"","content":"This week's preview:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1500\" height=\"960\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OKY2KKL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OKY2KKL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/OKY2KKL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><ul><li>Neither character-section really grabbed me here.</li> <li>A Children of Gaia Garou who's borderline-Pacifist...? That feels a bit on the nose...</li> <li>The other one... A &quot;Hungarian Baron&quot;...? Might as well call him Count Dracula and say that he lives in a castle... Another stereotypical idea here: The rich, influential Eastern European nobleman with evil designs for the world around him.</li> <li>The section also runs into the problem of ending up being more about this evil baron than the twin-sisters themselves. Who are they? What are they like when you interact with them? The way it's described, they might as well be a bunch of combat-robots.</li> <li>Can't help but notice that it feels like we're going back in time: A Shadow Lord who's Eastern European. And the Gehenna War preview revealed a Ministry/Followers of Set Elder from Egypt. It seems like with Juhana Pettersson's direction as lead-developer we're moving away from the idea of this being decidedly not a continuation.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T10:34:08-07:00","id":1540367,"title":"","content":"First of all; These sound pretty much as valid character concepts for Legacy as for W5.<br /> <br /> Second, Little Sister has no human identity... so what's her touchstone? Also, Death in Words sure is critical of a kid of a peaceful tribe.<br /> <br /> Agreed on the 'twins' being more about the Baron and the Baron being a stereotypical Evulz Lord. Also, given this setting it makes no sense for him to manage to capture identical-looking strangers who ALSO both changed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T12:39:39-07:00","id":1540380,"title":"","content":"After digesting the section a bit, I think the part that is most disappointing about both descriptions is that I think the environment these descriptions would feel most at home in would be Saturday-morning-cartoons. The plucky young teen girl who thinks violence is wrong and love can fix everything, the two twin-girls who not only are twins but are <i>exactly </i>alike - and they're psychotic killers. Except that deep down they want to break free and it's only because of that evil/manipulative father-figure in their lives that they have not. I mean, that girl and those twins would feel right at home in a Sailor Moon episode.<br /> <br /> Because you have that First Change with the girl where people get hurt or even killed... but where is the moment when she dealt with the innate Rage of being a Garou? After that first traumatic event, it seems to just disappear. She was all about love and sunshine before but beyond a change in scenery because of the events of her First Change, she's still all love and sunshine, it seems.<br /> <br /> Taking two twins and making them look <i>exactly </i>alike... that's just lame. And then the evil baron as well. That whole section wasn't a description of a possible path to being a Garou you want to present to players. It's a hackneyed attempt at a carboard-villain! And the section ignores the <i>only </i>interesting element: What do the twins think is going on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540367#post1540367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Death in Words sure is critical of a kid of a peaceful tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what that writing reminded me of? The Ahroun-section in the corebook. &quot;She's too dumb to use words like pacifist&quot; and ending the whole thing with &quot;Ugh.&quot;... Death-In-Word better be a teenager himself the way he sounds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T17:46:35-07:00","id":1540396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540367#post1540367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all; These sound pretty much as valid character concepts for Legacy as for W5.<br /> <br /> Second, Little Sister has no human identity... so what's her touchstone? Also, Death in Words sure is critical of a kid of a peaceful tribe.<br /> <br /> Agreed on the 'twins' being more about the Baron and the Baron being a stereotypical Evulz Lord. Also, given this setting it makes no sense for him to manage to capture identical-looking strangers who ALSO both changed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like it would be less of a stretch to have them actually be twins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T18:12:11-07:00","id":1540400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540380#post1540380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After digesting the section a bit, I think the part that is most disappointing about both descriptions is that I think the environment these descriptions would feel most at home in would be Saturday-morning-cartoons. The plucky young teen girl who thinks violence is wrong and love can fix everything, the two twin-girls who not only are twins but are <i>exactly </i>alike - and they're psychotic killers. Except that deep down they want to break free and it's only because of that evil/manipulative father-figure in their lives that they have not. I mean, that girl and those twins would feel right at home in a Sailor Moon episode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I feel like parawolf hear that criticisms of WoD 5e having less gonzo moments and addressing it in the most thoughtless way possible.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T23:09:02-07:00","id":1540414,"title":"","content":"Ok so Sister is just a Legacy Coggie stereotype.<br /> <br /> The twins are.......a ruse that falls apart in about 2 minutes flat the moment they are around someone in wolf-form or using Sensory Gifts? Cos they aren't really related and they will absolutely smell very different.<br /> <br /> Is the Baron supposed to be a Margrave pastiche?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T23:48:36-07:00","id":1540416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540414#post1540414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The twins are.......a ruse that falls apart in about 2 minutes flat the moment they are around someone in wolf-form or using Sensory Gifts? Cos they aren't really related and they will absolutely smell very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hoping the Baron at least invested in teaching them scent altering gifts.<br /> <br /> But once more, the gameplay intended seems like Legacy with extra limits put on it. Which I guess is good that the actual play hasn't changed. But it isn't taking advantage of the freedom W5 offers the PCs.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it other words, the corebook archetypes would not fit into the world Shattered Nation proposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T01:54:03-07:00","id":1540419,"title":"","content":"We see that the idea of this section is to describe example paths for how werewolves are inducted into Garou-society. And the &quot;twins&quot;-concept feels way too convoluted to be any kind of model for how this would usually go. Worse than that, it's complicated in some ways and quite bland in others. Like, the idea is that the twins are supposed to be a propaganda-weapon but then all there is to them is just &quot;Look, it's Ahroun-twins who fight good.&quot;. No prophecy or some tale of past glories are getting invoked. It's just the evil baron-guy saying &quot;I have twin-daughters who are both Ahroun and fight good.&quot;. That's lame.<br /> <br /> And it does bring up the lack of &quot;re-imagination&quot; again. This idea of the twins being a &quot;propaganda-weapon&quot; the Shadow Lords can use against the Silver Fangs: That imagines a type of setting with Tribes that are more similar to the legacy-editions and not this universalist &quot;Anybody anywhere can join any Tribe.&quot;-idea from the W5 corebook. Even stuff like the section believing that it's important for the baron to falsely claim that they're his daughters. That hints at how heredity would be the main-factor to undergoing First Change. If it were just the chaotic &quot;Anybody anywhere can be Kin who then later undergoes First Change.&quot;.<br /> <br /> So you get these sections where it does feel more like a continuation and the underlying principles are those from the legacy-editions. And it's like that until it suddenly is not as the worldbuilding swerves into this other direction. Of course, it's awfully convenient for the writers to rely on legacy-stuff to this degree without any responsibility to stay faithful to it or be invested in staying consistent. Calling the twins his daughters is somehow meaningful but W5 of course doesn't believe in heredity being a main-factor anymore and Kinfolk don't exist either. Anytime, there's something that breaks with established worldbuilding, they just can bring up the &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;-thing again. Meanwhile, they're doing stuff like &quot;Of course, there's still the same-old rivalry between Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs.&quot; or &quot;How are Septs organized? Actually, it's exactly the same way as before, here's the copy-pasted list of all the Sept-positions...&quot;. Rather than &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, W5 is more like this shoddy mixture that is neither invested in being its own thing nor in being a faithful continuation. It's a game of chance with whoever the writer is just picking and choosing on a whim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T02:14:56-07:00","id":1540421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540419#post1540419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'm going with the head cannon that W5 setting is fake and is actually a poorly researched torture prison that Albecht was stuffed into as punishment for his part in cancelling the apocalypse and WtE is the real world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though On the topic of WtE how would you compare the lore shown in the preview materials to Shattered nation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T08:06:09-07:00","id":1540432,"title":"","content":"If anything W5 has the exact opposite problem to V5, in that the creators seem to have had a lack of vision rather than an overly specific ones. Yes it has some of the strange symptoms but the only thing the creators of the core seems to have agreed on is that the Get are baddies.<br /> <br /> The direction I would have expected is not 'rebuild the Nation' but more 'oh fuck we're useless' where the relative progress of the last decade or so is acknowledged.and Garou have to acknowledge that ordinary humans have somehow made more progress than them.<br /> <br /> (Yes we're still going to have to love with the effects of Climate Change and ecosystem destruction, but we're slowly crawling away from the worst consequences.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:22:45-07:00","id":1540453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540421#post1540421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though On the topic of WtE how would you compare the lore shown in the preview materials to Shattered nation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have purposefully not delved too deeply into the particulars of WtE because I want to wait for its release and then I'll review it here as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Then again, it's hard to imagine that it will be worse than W5. The people working on it are fans of WtA, they don't have Paradox breathing down their necks and they don't have somebody on the team like Karim Muammar who's obsessed with &quot;Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540432#post1540432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything W5 has the exact opposite problem to V5, in that the creators seem to have had a lack of vision rather than an overly specific ones. Yes it has some of the strange symptoms but the only thing the creators of the core seems to have agreed on is that the Get are baddies.<br /> <br /> The direction I would have expected is not 'rebuild the Nation' but more 'oh fuck we're useless' where the relative progress of the last decade or so is acknowledged.and Garou have to acknowledge that ordinary humans have somehow made more progress than them.<br /> <br /> (Yes we're still going to have to love with the effects of Climate Change and ecosystem destruction, but we're slowly crawling away from the worst consequences.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are so many weird decisions (or non-decisions) that have been made with that W5 corebook that don't add up. You had all these basic setting-elements that got the &quot;Who knows&quot;-treatment. And from that, you get stuff like mentioning that one strain of thought is that the Garou Nation never existed in the first place (which aligns with the section of the W5 corebook wondering how long the Garou Nation even lasted). And then you have that strain of thought in W5 where humanity is the real bad guy and actually if humanity were just a little bit nicer, the Wyrm and its minions would be irrelevant. Because the decision was made that the Umbra should be less important in W5 and PCs should be more focused on humanity.<br /> <br /> And now these writers working for Renegade with a new lead-developer have to somehow turn all these various ideas into something that makes sense - or try to anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T12:28:45-07:00","id":1540457,"title":"","content":"The vision was to add angst to W:tA because the designers couldn't live with other WoD games not being Vampire. When several different ways of this fell through, they pushed the reset button... and then added in a bunch of awful shit (see: everything involving the Fenrir) even though the reset button would have kept it from ever being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T23:34:54-07:00","id":1540499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540453#post1540453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have purposefully not delved too deeply into the particulars of WtE because I want to wait for its release and then I'll review it here as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Then again, it's hard to imagine that it will be worse than W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I wish you luck on the review<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Though I should mention that in contrast to how W5's &quot;Who cares&quot; approach to lore, WtE preview material I've got actually includes a section the history of the garou nation from it's founding to the current day including how the nation actually fell:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540021#post1540021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y1kveps.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/My9km4N.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>And it just took about 8 whole pages to lay out that info.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Get of Fenris=Nazis&quot;. </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I think it's better to take inspiration from Purgatory and reimagine the cult as a political movement that can be adopted by garou of any tribe rather than a single fallen tribe since I think it would make for a credible and insidious threat. (like Cof might not even be the main organisation of this ideology but a convenient lighting rod to divert attention away from they true operations and convent place to station all the idiots )<br /> <br /> And to be honest in that form they would be a more apporate threat in WtE since by all indication this book is shaping much more political than W5. Like we already got hints of political conflicts in the two halves of the group nation. from heathbound fight for kinfolk and crinos rights laying the foundation for the split to the Glass Walkers expulsion from the budding eastcon forcing to settle with the westcons. And undoubly there instance of political conflicts in this and future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T01:31:48-07:00","id":1540502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540499#post1540499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I think it's better to take inspiration from Purgatory and reimagine the cult as a political movement that can be adopted by garou of any tribe rather than a single fallen tribe since I think it would make for a credible and insidious threat. (like Cof might not even be the main organisation of this ideology but a convenient lighting rod to divert attention away from they true operations and convent place to station all the idiots )</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. That version does make more sense. Having them be this cultish movement/faction that any Garou can join also makes more sense in the context of how Hauglosk works. Because really, at the end of the day what even is the difference between a Pack of Fenrir in W5 and a Pack led by some other random Tribe's Garou who's consumed by Hauglosk? Between Hauglosk being a general issue for all Garou and the Cult of Fenris having no special kind of Hauglosk, there's really no in-universe reason for the Cult of Fenris to be this one particular Tribe that has somehow fallen to Hauglosk on a tribal level. Of course, we know the one thing that did make them exceptional was one of the developers being obsessed with the idea of turning them into Nazis/antagonists. It would've made far more sense to either rework them a la Galestalkers and Ghost Council or maybe even explain that the Tribe has formed splinter-groups and the non-Hauglosk-faction of the Tribe is playable.<br /> <br /> But alas... I'll just take it how it comes and note the discrepancies and contradictions in the worldbuilding in my reviews.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T02:43:25-07:00","id":1540504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540502#post1540502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. That version does make more sense. Having them be this cultish movement/faction that any Garou can join also makes more sense in the context of how Hauglosk works. Because really, at the end of the day what even is the difference between a Pack of Fenrir in W5 and a Pack led by some other random Tribe's Garou who's consumed by Hauglosk? Between Hauglosk being a general issue for all Garou and the Cult of Fenris having no special kind of Hauglosk, there's really no in-universe reason for the Cult of Fenris to be this one particular Tribe that has somehow fallen to Hauglosk on a tribal level. Of course, we know the one thing that did make them exceptional was one of the developers being obsessed with the idea of turning them into Nazis/antagonists. It would've made far more sense to either rework them a la Galestalkers and Ghost Council or maybe even explain that the Tribe has formed splinter-groups and the non-Hauglosk-faction of the Tribe is playable.<br /> <br /> But alas... I'll just take it how it comes and note the discrepancies and contradictions in the worldbuilding in my reviews.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think it's an end result of taking away as much politics as possible from the setting. Writing an insidious movement that prey on the natural territorials instacts of the garou is evidently too hard for the devs so they just stick wtih a tribe that somehow fallen and not give any answers on why they are fallen . And even then Purgatory provides a foundation for a legitimate answer. They totem fallen to rage causing a spiritual imbalance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T10:14:42-07:00","id":1540847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1250\" height=\"800\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3F4A3bI.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3F4A3bI.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/3F4A3bI.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><ul><li>The description is overly general. Especially because the mechanic actually linked to Touchstones are the three recovery mechanics that can be used once per chapter and harm befalling them leading to Frenzy or Harano checks. That's what should have been discussed here instead. The general stuff had already been covered by the corebook.</li> <li>Only human Touchstones... sigh</li> <li>You know, that relative of a Garou that happens to be immune to Delirium. Man, wouldn't it be nice if we had an in-universe term for that...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T12:18:06-07:00","id":1540849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540847#post1540847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Snip-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, there are two things that are in conflict with each other;<br /> <br /> -Borrowing uncle's cabin for a moot indicates there are no better spaces FOR a moot to be held.<br /> <br /> -Mention of the Veil mattering.<br /> <br /> If you have a setting where you have to borrow your uncle's cabin, then at that point the veil is not your biggest problem. Not to mention, the corebook said the Litany doesn't matter anymore.<br /> <br /> I know I complained about the Litany not mattering before, but I want to make my stance clear; What matters to me is a consistent setting. IF the core says most younger garou don't care about the Litany, then PLEASE don't turn around in the next book and say it matters.<br /> <br /> If this book starts with &quot;Ignore core's takes&quot;, THEN I'm fine with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T20:21:58-07:00","id":1540872,"title":"","content":"Ok...so...<br /> 90% of that was just restating what's in the Core. And Touchstones...if you choose to use them cos mechanically they&quot;re nothing in W5...should be tailored to individual characters so listing a bunch of extremely generic examples is useless..<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's 2 wasted pages....<br /> <br /> Why is The Veil not capitalised? And yeah...Kinfolk. Lets see if Gaian Cults gives us Kinfolk with Gifts and Rites back as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T20:41:18-07:00","id":1540873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540872#post1540872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok...so...<br /> 90% of that was just restating what's in the Core. And Touchstones...if you choose to use them cos mechanically they&quot;re nothing in W5...should be tailored to individual characters so listing a bunch of extremely generic examples is useless..<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's 2 wasted pages....<br /> <br /> Why is The Veil not capitalised? And yeah...Kinfolk. Lets see if Gaian Cults gives us Kinfolk with Gifts and Rites back as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it is not repeating the core, it is contradicting it in a way that brings the old canon back while making the core's new one actively impossible.<br /> <br /> I also want to note something; &quot;Touchstone is a game term, the garou don't use it as they see it as unlike them&quot; (paraphrased.) So, Touchstone is something that has no in-character name and functions nearly purely as a mechanic? Then why is it here? A Touchstone doesn't offer anything that your basic kinfolk ally or contact wouldn't in Legacy.<br /> <br /> Vampires need Touchstones, because their existence is unnatural and the Touchstones serve as a link to sanity. That is not the case with the garou, being one IS part of your nature. How you behave is how you should behave, you don't need a connection to humanity/lupinity to reinforce your relationship with something you never were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-21T23:39:24-07:00","id":1540878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540849#post1540849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> -Mention of the Veil mattering.<br /> <br /> If you have a setting where you have to borrow your uncle's cabin, then at that point the veil is not your biggest problem. Not to mention, the corebook said the Litany doesn't matter anymore.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly of all the Litany tenants you can break then &quot;Do not lift Veil&quot; is one of the safest one the garou can break, strictly speaking there no supernatural consequences for breaking the veil other than retaliation from fellow garou and fear of your friends and family getting targeted by aforementioned or the servants of the wyrm. <br /> <br /> Of course, if the nation fallen then a garou will not fear such retaliation. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile in the WtE verse I actually headcannon that at least some septs in the Eastern Concordat actually toyed around with the idea of lifting the Veil because they beleave that keeping humanity ignorant of the spitural world is doing more harm than good in the long run and that if they just educate the masses on why they have to fight Pentex and the Wrym then they will turn ageist them and the Age of Balance will truly begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T06:10:20-07:00","id":1540886,"title":"","content":"I feel like we're now at a point where the writers can't decide whether the standard-scenario for W5 is the PC-Pack with one or two other Garou and/or one other Pack around at most with the Litany/Septs/Garou-Nation not mattering much or if we're just going back to how things used to be with Septs, mutliple Packs around and the LItany and stuff like Moots mattering a lot. The problem is that you can't do both of these things at the same time. Also, why would the Garou-Nation be considered to be fallen when two isolated Packs feel the need to still commit to Garou-traditions/rituals like doing a Moot and therefore are fine with using locations like some random cabin?<br /> <br /> The way Touchstones end up being described feels more like a burden than anything else. It's like somebody forced the issue on the game and then no writer ever came up with a justification for why exactly they're in the game. According to the text, Garou in the setting don't care about Touchstones and on a game-level they also simply exist because somebody somewhere decided that all WOD5E games need to have Touchstones. Without any thematic relevance, Touchstones just end up being some random human who's occasionally an inconvenience and sometimes a &quot;nice shoulder to cry on&quot; (recovery mechanics) and them getting hurt triggers Frenzy or Harano checks. The text only mentions how Garou would lose themselves to Rage without Touchstones... which isn't a thing in the system. It's simply assumed that Garou-PC need a connection to humanity. And it just feels lame to see it laid out like that when CofD 2E should've offered more than enough examples that Touchstones are better off being thematically flavored at least if that mechanic just has to be included.<br /> <br /> It also comes off as cheap if the Gaian cults end up being this assembly of humans who worship Gaia and in return some become immune to Delirium and their children are very likely to be Kin (future Garou). At that point, W5 jumped through all these hoops with Kin only to come around and re-introduce Kinfolk again. Except the explanation makes less sense now. Both Kin and Delirium-immune humans... just happen. At least Kinfolk and Wolf-Blooded people had a place in the setting. Here with Kin and Delirium-immunity it's just there because the ST said so because within the setting there's neither rhyme nor reason to it.<br /> <br /> The issue of the text feeling like the writer was just using different words to restate superficial explanations from the corebook has come up two times already now. Hopefully this isn't too big of an issue with the book. They should've just done W5.5 corebook instead if the writers at Renegade feel like basic elements in the W5 corebook need to be revisited and revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T16:34:02-07:00","id":1540916,"title":"","content":"Touchstones.....mostly....kinda...sometimes...work for V5, in W5 they only really interact with the mechanics to allow you to flick a switch from PTSD to Fash and in H5 they do literally nothing.<br /> <br /> As a mechanic its very much just forcing playstyles.....people who were going to invest in their background characters would have done so anyway and those who weren't will essentially just ignore the Touchstone until the ST uses it as a club.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-22T18:06:36-07:00","id":1540923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1540886#post1540886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also comes off as cheap if the Gaian cults end up being this assembly of humans who worship Gaia and in return some become immune to Delirium and their children are very likely to be Kin (future Garou). At that point, W5 jumped through all these hoops with Kin only to come around and re-introduce Kinfolk again. Except the explanation makes less sense now. Both Kin and Delirium-immune humans... just happen. At least Kinfolk and Wolf-Blooded people had a place in the setting. Here with Kin and Delirium-immunity it's just there because the ST said so because within the setting there's neither rhyme nor reason to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contrast that with Mandusarts last project, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Heathbound</a> which do have a focus on the knfolk relationship with the garou and of course the existence of the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Heathbound</a> as a tribe and how the other tribes react to they presence in the nation.<br /> <br /> And it would seem that elements of kinfolk rights carries over to they next project WtE since well kinfolk rights is a major factor that caused the split in the first place and the glass walkers are actually left the Easten Concordat partly because of troubled relationship with they kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 08-25-2024, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T17:42:06-07:00","id":1541152,"title":"","content":"This week's preview: <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1449\" height=\"927\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WAf3EJx.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WAf3EJx.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/WAf3EJx.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> I won't offer my thoughts on this because <b>the preview-pdf is out</b>. It has 146 pages. So expect my review on it tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Some things I saw skimming the pdf:<ul><li>Like predicted: It has the &quot;You're Albrecht's newest BFF&quot;-Loresheet. All the other six Loresheets are also &quot;You know this one specific Garou&quot;-Loresheets, like, for example, a Shanghai taikonaut (Chinese astronaut) who had her First Change in space.</li> <li>It seems like it's very light on actual worldbuilding. It's more about example-Septs and regarding the Garou-Nation it just has a bunch of quotes from various characters.</li> <li>Pack-Type is also what I hoped it would be as it is obviously an attempt to take Coterie-rules and put them into W5.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T19:36:08-07:00","id":1541158,"title":"","content":"Those Septs are massive compared to the Sept composure laid out in the Core.......Renegades really kinda doing their own thing I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T20:46:24-07:00","id":1541165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541158#post1541158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Septs are massive compared to the Sept composure laid out in the Core.......Renegades really kinda doing their own thing I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honstly I think they're making the Septs in to lodge equivalents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T22:49:51-07:00","id":1541170,"title":"","content":"Is there any reasonable way in which a taikonaut changing in space won't end up killing everyone on board including themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:12:23-07:00","id":1541173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541170#post1541170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reasonable way in which a taikonaut changing in space won't end up killing everyone on board including themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. But apparently it happened....so either the Chinese Space Agency knows about Werewolves....cos even if there were no witnesses left alive there are cameras fricking everywhere on manned orbital equipment.....or the Technocracy stepped in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:57:19-07:00","id":1541177,"title":"","content":"I do recall folks on the official Discord remarking that W5 Garou can survive literally anything short of complete bodily destruction.as long as no silver is involved...so even if the capsule was destroyed she can just float out there in space not asphyxiating until she falls into low orbit and begins re-entry then all she has to do is not burn up completely and not get atomised on impact....which might actually work RAW...<br /> but is extremely goofy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:58:41-07:00","id":1541178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541170#post1541170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reasonable way in which a taikonaut changing in space won't end up killing everyone on board including themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's one of those instances where they manage to step sideways immediately, as with some Theurge backgrounds, maybe. But then they have to hide from the rest of the world for the rest of their lives or get very good at fake identities, because anyone seeing them in Homid would naturally start asking questions about just how said taikonaut got back to Earth. So, even without death, a major danger to the veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-28T23:59:43-07:00","id":1541179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541177#post1541177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do recall folks on the official Discord remarking that W5 Garou can survive literally anything short of complete bodily destruction.as long as no silver is involved...so even if the capsule was destroyed she can just float out there in space not asphyxiating until she falls into low orbit and begins re-entry then all she has to do is not burn up completely and not get atomised on impact....which might actually work RAW...<br /> but is extremely goofy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to rake anyone over the coals for this if they ever bring up Crinos mini golf. No mercy, no compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T00:01:07-07:00","id":1541180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541165#post1541165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honstly I think they're making the Septs in to lodge equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. The two example Septs in the preview are basically just a standard Legacy Bonegnawer/Coggie Sept and a typical Black Fury + Fenrir/Strider or Coggie Sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T01:00:50-07:00","id":1541183,"title":"","content":"Oh look, as per WoD5 tradition, gotta make direct reference to a current thing. About the sinking of a boat to Italy, I mean. Why do they pick the absolutely worst ones that are so specific to a certain area that they require you to be from that area to even use it? And also ones that are such hot-button issues that most players of that location would feel extremely uncomfortable using in their games...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T09:27:16-07:00","id":1541200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541178#post1541178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's one of those instances where they manage to step sideways immediately, as with some Theurge backgrounds, maybe. But then they have to hide from the rest of the world for the rest of their lives or get very good at fake identities, because anyone seeing them in Homid would naturally start asking questions about just how said taikonaut got back to Earth. So, even without death, a major danger to the veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the same, but then I remembered that the Umbra is now super-hostile, so that's a pretty baddass Garou to make the whole journey back to surface on their own at First Change.<br /> <br /> Was that a result of taikonaut training?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-29T23:26:48-07:00","id":1541222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541200#post1541200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the same, but then I remembered that the Umbra is now super-hostile, so that's a pretty baddass Garou to make the whole journey back to surface on their own at First Change.<br /> <br /> Was that a result of taikonaut training?</div> </div> </div> </div>I almost want to suggest that they may be dialing back the Umbra restrictions. But only almost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T06:02:10-07:00","id":1541224,"title":"","content":"Nah, if they were dialing back the Umbra restrictions I'd say we we're only six books away from them bringing Gnosis back, and two fuel stats is too much for the nWW line heads to wrap their heads around.<br /> <br /> That said I could see a space-based first change working if the Garou was in a small or solo vehicle were cameras getting destroyed quickly is viable. There will still be a lot of questions if they're not along, probably 'what the fuck did you do to make those bite marks, and how did you expect to get away with it.<br /> <br /> Probably the best case scenario is having your first change on the way back from space. Even then there's a good chance you'll want to disappoint forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T11:16:37-07:00","id":1541238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541224#post1541224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, if they were dialing back the Umbra restrictions I'd say we we're only six books away from them bringing Gnosis back, and two fuel stats is too much for the nWW line heads to wrap their heads around.<br /> <br /> That said I could see a space-based first change working if the Garou was in a small or solo vehicle were cameras getting destroyed quickly is viable. There will still be a lot of questions if they're not along, probably 'what the fuck did you do to make those bite marks, and how did you expect to get away with it.<br /> <br /> Probably the best case scenario is having your first change on the way back from space. Even then there's a good chance you'll want to disappoint forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing everyone and being filmed are huge Veil problems, but not what makes this impossible.<br /> <br /> The real problem is that spaceships are really, <b>REALLY </b>sensitive equipment. Unless the Garou crosses the Gauntlet, it would have to be un unexpectedly calm First Change, where they don't break anything in the tight space they have, for the Garou to not destroy their chances at going back home in the same vessel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T12:14:02-07:00","id":1541240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541238#post1541238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Killing everyone and being filmed are huge Veil problems, but not what makes this impossible.<br /> <br /> The real problem is that spaceships are really, <b>REALLY </b>sensitive equipment. Unless the Garou crosses the Gauntlet, it would have to be un unexpectedly calm First Change, where they don't break anything in the tight space they have, for the Garou to not destroy their chances at going back home in the same vessel.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the hockey player passage, recycled in space! How did the hockey uniforms help? Who knows! How did the spaceship hold up? Dunno lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T14:02:31-07:00","id":1541243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1539594-w5-shattered-nation-preview?p=1541183#post1541183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh look, as per WoD5 tradition, gotta make direct reference to a current thing. About the sinking of a boat to Italy, I mean. Why do they pick the absolutely worst ones that are so specific to a certain area that they require you to be from that area to even use it? And also ones that are such hot-button issues that most players of that location would feel extremely uncomfortable using in their games...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's not &quot;the sinking of a boat&quot;: there's thousands of people drowning each year in the Mediterranean, and the Libya-Italy sea lane is the main venue of illegal immigration from Africa to Europe. There's boats arriving in Sicily basically every day.<br /> <br /> So, it's not some obscure fact only locals are aware of, it's basically the European &quot;Mexican Border&quot; issue, but much worse in terms of lost lives, and most politically conscious Europeans probably have at least passing knowledge of the issue.<br /> <br /> And personally I'm very glad they are bringing attention to this. Why should &quot;most players of that location&quot; feel uncomfortable using it in their games? It's classic WW of bringing attention to something very dark and very much happening now, and in these two pages t's done in an absolutely respectful manner.<br /> <br /> It's really not a taboo to speak of people drowning in the Mediterranean here in Italy, it's one of our main political issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T20:13:46-07:00","id":1541259,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Please refrain from double posting in an attempt to get around the spam filter. It doesn't get your post out there any quicker and it makes more work for the moderators. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}